\n\
Now, my plan for this turn:\n\
- I have 4 untapped lands\n\
- Dwynen's Elite (1G) is an Elf that makes a token since I control another Elf → triggers Warmaster too!\n\
- Skyway Sniper (G) is another Elf with reach\n\
- I could cast both for 3 mana total, getting 2 Warmaster triggers (2 more tokens)\n\
\n\
That gives me a wide board. Then I can use Band Together next turn to deal with Harbinger if needed. Or I could hold up Titanic Growth for a combat trick.\n\
\n\
Let me think about Harbinger — it's 4/3 and attacks next turn. I need to be able to block or remove it. Band Together with 2 creatures dealing their power could handle it.\n\
\n\
Best line: Cast Dwynen's Elite (1G) → triggers Warmaster (token), Dwynen's Elite ETB (token). Then cast Skyway Sniper (G) → triggers Warmaster again (another token). That's 3 mana, I still have 1 left for Elven Bow if I want. But Skyway Sniper has reach so it can block flyers.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me cast Dwynen's Elite first, then Skyway Sniper. That gives me tons of bodies.",
