      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "My Turn 5! I drew Roots of Wisdom. Opponent played a Thriving Grove on their turn and didn't attack with Harbinger (maybe they're waiting for more setup with Adventuring Gear + landfall).\n\
\n\
Now, I have 7 creatures all untapped, 4 lands untapped. Opponent has Garruk's Harbinger 4/3 and Oashra Cultivator 0/3.\n\
\n\
If I attack with everything, Harbinger can eat one of my creatures (it's 4/3). The 0/3 Cultivator can block but deals 0 damage. I should think about what to hold back to block Harbinger next turn.\n\
\n\
Harbinger is 4/3 — I need at least 4 toughness to survive blocking, or I can chump. If I equip Elven Bow to something, it gets +1/+2 and reach. Dwynen's Elite would become 3/4 with reach — can block and survive against the 4/3! But equipping costs 3 mana.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the attack. I want to keep back some blockers for Harbinger. If I attack with most creatures and keep Dwynen's Elite back, I can equip the bow to her after combat and block Harbinger next turn.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually I should consider: if I attack with everything, they can block with Harbinger (4/3) and Cultivator (0/3). With 7 attackers (total power = 2+1+1+1+1+1+1 = 8), minus whatever they block, that's a lot of damage.\n\
\n\
Optimal line: Attack with everything except Dwynen's Elite (hold back as future blocker for Harbinger). That's 6 attackers with total power 6 (1+1+1+1+1+1). Opponent can block one with Cultivator, so 5 damage through.\n\
\n\
Actually, Harbinger is untapped so it can block too. They could block 2 creatures. So 4 damage through with 6 attackers. \n\
\n\
Let me attack with all except Dwynen's Elite to preserve my biggest creature for blocking.",
