      "reasoning": "Turn 6! I drew Wildheart Invoker (4/3 for 2GG). Let me think about my plays:\n\
\n\
1. **Elvish Warmaster (1G)** - Gets back my token engine, creates a token when another elf enters\n\
2. **Wildheart Invoker (2GG)** - Big 4/3 body, but the 8-mana ability is too expensive to matter\n\
3. **Band Together (2G)** - Could kill the Beast token or even target Garruk directly? No, it targets a creature.\n\
4. **Elven Bow** - Equip ability\n\
\n\
I should cast Elvish Warmaster first (1G), then I'll have 2 mana left. I could equip Elven Bow (3 mana, but I only have 2 left). So I can't equip this turn.\n\
\n\
Actually, with 4 lands, I should prioritize killing Garruk. If I cast Warmaster (1G), I still have 2 mana open. Then I attack — I need to send enough power at Garruk to kill it (3 loyalty). They have Beast 3/3 (sick, can't block) and Cultivator 0/3 to block. \n\
\n\
My creatures: Dwynen's Elite 2/2, 3x Elf tokens 1/1, Rejuvenator 1/1, Skyway Sniper 1/2, and new Warmaster 2/2 (summoning sick).\n\
\n\
Non-sick attackers: Dwynen's Elite 2/2, 3x tokens 1/1, Rejuvenator 1/1, Skyway Sniper 1/2 = total power 8.\n\
\n\
Opponent can block with Cultivator 0/3 only (Beast is sick). I can send Dwynen's Elite + 1 token at Garruk (3 damage = kills it), and the rest at face (4 damage to opponent, going to 12).\n\
\n\
Let me cast Warmaster first for the token value, then attack.",
