\n\
Plan:\n\
- Send Dwynen's Elite (2/2) + 1 Elf token (1/1) at Garruk = 3 damage, kills it\n\
- Send remaining 4 creatures at opponent: 3 tokens (1/1 each) + Rejuvenator (1/1) + Skyway Sniper (1/2) = wait, I already counted one token at Garruk\n\
\n\
Let me recalculate: \n\
- At Garruk: Dwynen's Elite (2) + Elf Token (1) = 3 power → kills Garruk\n\
- At face: Rejuvenator (1) + 2 Elf Tokens (1+1) + Skyway Sniper (1) = 4 power\n\
- Opponent blocks one with Cultivator (0/3), so 3 damage gets through\n\
\n\
Actually, I can just attack all 6 at the face and ignore Garruk... but Garruk at 3 loyalty is dangerous. If they +1 it next turn, the 3/3 Beast becomes 6/6 trample and attacks. That's devastating. I need to kill Garruk.\n\
\n\
Let me attack all at Garruk first — no wait, I want to split. I'll send some at Garruk and the rest at face.\n\
\n\
Hmm, the declare attackers interface might not let me split between player and planeswalker. Let me just declare all attackers and then assign targets.",
