      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Turn 7! Drew Reclamation Sage (2/1 for 2G, destroys an artifact/enchantment on ETB). 13 life vs 16, I need to be aggressive.\n\
\n\
My options:\n\
1. **Reclamation Sage (2G)** - It's an Elf! Triggers Warmaster to create a token. Can destroy their Adventuring Gear. 2/1 body.\n\
2. **Wildheart Invoker (2GG)** - Big 4/3, but not an Elf so no Warmaster trigger. Costs all 4 mana.\n\
3. **Band Together (2G)** - Removal spell. Could kill the Beast token (pick 2 creatures dealing power to it).\n\
4. **Elven Bow** - Create a 1/1 Elf token (2 mana) or equip.\n\
\n\
The best play is Reclamation Sage:\n\
- Triggers Warmaster → creates an Elf Warrior token\n\
- Destroys Adventuring Gear (eliminates landfall pump threat)\n\
- Leaves 1 mana open for Elven Bow activation? No, Bow costs 2 to create token or 3 to equip.\n\
\n\
With 4 lands: Rec Sage costs 3, leaving 1 mana. Not enough for anything else.\n\
\n\
Or I could play Wildheart Invoker (4/3) for all 4 mana — it's a much bigger body for attacking. But no synergy with Warmaster.\n\
\n\
Actually, Rec Sage + Warmaster token = 2 new creatures (Rec Sage 2/1 + token 1/1). That's +3 power added. Wildheart Invoker = +4 power but only 1 body.\n\
\n\
I think Reclamation Sage is better: removes Adventuring Gear (their only equipment), triggers Warmaster, and it's a solid Elf for the team. Let me play it.",
