      "reasoning": "6 available attackers! Let me think about whether to hold back Warmaster for blocking purposes. They have Beast 3/3 that will untap next turn.\n\
\n\
If I keep Warmaster back to block Beast next turn, I send 5 power (5 creatures), they block 1 with Cultivator, 4 damage through. Opponent goes to 12.\n\
\n\
If I attack all 6, that's 7 power, they block 1, ~5-6 damage through. Opponent goes to 10-11. But then I have no good blocker for Beast next turn.\n\
\n\
However, I also have Band Together (2G) and Wildheart Invoker (2GG) in hand. Next turn with 5 lands, I can cast Band Together to kill the Beast, or play Invoker as a big blocker. I think going all-in on attacks is better — I need to pressure them.\n\
\n\
Actually, Warmaster's activated ability (6 mana total, {5}{G}) gives all elves +1/+1 and deathtouch. I can't afford that yet. And Warmaster's passive creates tokens — it's very valuable. But we need to close this game out.\n\
\n\
Let me attack all and plan to use Band Together to kill Beast next turn if needed.",
