      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I can block with Reclamation Sage (2/1) or the new Elf token (1/1)! They're not tapped since they were summoning sick and didn't attack.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Block Beast 3/3 with Rec Sage (2/1): Sage dies, Beast takes 2 damage (survives at 3/1), I take 0. Lose a 2/1.\n\
- Block Beast 3/3 with Elf Token (1/1): Token dies, Beast takes 1 damage (survives at 3/2), I take 0. Lose a 1/1.\n\
- Double block with both: Both die, Beast takes 3 damage and dies! That removes the Beast permanently.\n\
- No block: Take 3 damage, go to 10.\n\
\n\
Double blocking kills the Beast! That's huge — removes their main threat. I lose a 1/1 token and a 2/1 Rec Sage, but the Sage has already done its job (destroyed Adventuring Gear). Killing the Beast is worth it.\n\
\n\
Wait, Beast is 3/3. Rec Sage (2/1) + Token (1/1) = 3 power total. Beast deals 3 damage — I assign 2 to Sage (killing it) and 1 to Token (killing it). Both blockers die. Beast takes 3 damage total, which kills it.\n\
\n\
Let's double block!",
