      "reasoning": "Beast is dead! Both my blockers killed it. Excellent trade. I lost an Elf token and Rec Sage (which already did its job) to remove their biggest recurring threat.\n\
\n\
Turn 8! Drew a Forest. I'm at 13 life, they're at 11. I have 6 creatures, they just have Canopy Baloth 4/3 and Oashra Cultivator 0/3.\n\
\n\
My board: 3 Elf tokens (1/1), Rejuvenator (1/1), Warmaster (2/2), Skyway Sniper (1/2) = 7 power\n\
With 4 lands + Forest to play = 5 lands.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
1. Play Forest → Cast Wildheart Invoker (2GG) = 4/3 body. 5 mana used, 0 left.\n\
2. Play Forest → Cast Band Together (2G) to kill Canopy Baloth. Use 2 creatures to deal power to it. Need 4 damage to kill 4/3 Baloth. Warmaster (2) + Rec Sage... Sage is dead. Warmaster (2) + Skyway Sniper (1) = 3. Not enough! Warmaster (2) + Rejuvenator (1) = 3. Also not enough. I need 4 power combined to kill Baloth with Band Together and I can't get it.\n\
\n\
Actually, if I play Wildheart Invoker (4/3) first, then I could use Band Together with Invoker (4) + anything to kill Baloth, but I wouldn't have mana for both.\n\
\n\
Best plan: Play Forest, play Wildheart Invoker (4/3). Attack with everything. They can only block with Cultivator (0/3).\n\
\n\
That gives me: 3 tokens (3) + Rejuvenator (1) + Warmaster (2) + Sniper (1) = 7 power attacking. Invoker is sick. They block 1 with Cultivator, 6+ gets through. They go from 11 to 5 or lower!\n\
\n\
Wait, but Canopy Baloth can also block. It's marked as \"sick\" — was it just played? Yes, they played it turn 7. It entered tapped... no, sick means summoning sickness. By turn 8 it should... wait, it still says sick. Let me check.\n\
\n\
They played it last turn (their turn 7) so it would have summoning sickness during their turn but should be able to block on MY turn 8. \"Sick\" might just be the display. Creatures can always block even with summoning sickness.\n\
\n\
So blockers: Canopy Baloth 4/3 + Oashra Cultivator 0/3. That's two blockers. If Baloth blocks Warmaster (2/2), Warmaster dies and Baloth survives. Bad. If they block a token, Baloth kills it.\n\
\n\
Hmm, with Band Together I could kill the Baloth before combat. Forest → 5 lands. Band Together costs 2G. I need 2 creatures to deal ≥4 damage. Warmaster (2) + any 1/1 = 3. Not enough for 4. Warmaster (2) + Sniper (1) = 3. Still short.\n\
\n\
But wait — if I equip Elven Bow to something first? Elven Bow equips for {1}{G}. If I equip to Warmaster, it becomes 3/3. Then Band Together with Warmaster (3) + anything (1) = 4 damage, kills Baloth!\n\
\n\
Sequence: Play Forest (5 lands). Equip Elven Bow to Warmaster (1G, 2 lands used, 3 left). Cast Band Together (2G, 3 lands used). Target: Warmaster (3) + Sniper (1) deal 4 damage to Canopy Baloth (4/3). Baloth dies!\n\
\n\
Then attack with everything except... wait, Band Together doesn't tap the creatures. So all my creatures can still attack! And opponent only has Cultivator 0/3 as a blocker.\n\
\n\
Attack with 6 creatures (Warmaster 3/3, Sniper 1/2, Rejuvenator 1/1, 3 tokens 1/1 each) = 8 power. They block 1 with Cultivator (can absorb up to 3 damage but deals 0). Best case 7-8 damage through. They go from 11 to 3-4!\n\
\n\
This is a great line. Let me execute it.",
