      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Elven Bow: Equip costs {3}. Not {1}{G}. So to equip to Warmaster costs 3 mana. Then Band Together costs 3 mana (2G). That's 6 total but I only have 5 lands. Can't do both!\n\
\n\
Alternatives:\n\
1. Equip Bow to Warmaster (3 mana), Warmaster becomes 3/4 reach. Then I have 2 mana left — not enough for Band Together (3 mana).\n\
2. Cast Band Together (3 mana), using Warmaster (2) + Sniper (1) = 3 power. But Baloth is 4/3, needs 4 damage. Only 3 isn't enough!\n\
3. Cast Wildheart Invoker (4 mana, 2GG). 4/3 body, 1 mana left.\n\
4. Equip Bow to Warmaster (3 mana), attack with Warmaster 3/4. If they block with Baloth 4/3, Warmaster has 4 toughness and survives! Warmaster deals 3 to Baloth, Baloth deals 4 to Warmaster (dies since 4=4 toughness). Both trade! That's... actually Warmaster at 3/4 takes 4 damage and dies (4 damage ≥ 4 toughness). Hmm.\n\
\n\
Wait: Warmaster with Bow = 2+1/2+2 = 3/4. Baloth is 4/3. In combat: Warmaster 3 deals lethal to Baloth (3 ≥ 3 toughness), Baloth 4 deals lethal to Warmaster (4 ≥ 4 toughness). Both die. But I lose Warmaster which is terrible.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Don't worry about Baloth, just play Wildheart Invoker and attack with everything. If they block with Baloth, they can kill one creature but I still push through a lot of damage. Or I can hold back Warmaster.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the total attack:\n\
- 6 creatures: Warmaster (2), Sniper (1), Rejuvenator (1), 3 tokens (1 each) = 8 power\n\
- Defenders: Baloth (4/3) and Cultivator (0/3)\n\
- They block Warmaster with Baloth: Warmaster dies, Baloth takes 2 (lives). I lose my best creature.\n\
- They block a 1/1 with Baloth: Token dies. \n\
- They block a 1/1 with Cultivator: Token dies.\n\
- Best case: They block 2 tokens (one with Baloth, one with Cultivator). 6 power gets through. They go to 5.\n\
\n\
Actually, I should be smarter. Let me play Wildheart Invoker (4/3 body, sick) and then attack with the 6 non-sick creatures. The Invoker doesn't attack but adds future pressure. Then I have Warmaster as the most valuable — if they block Warmaster with Baloth, I lose a key piece.\n\
\n\
Better plan: Play Invoker (4 mana), keep 1 mana open. Attack with everyone except Warmaster. Send 5 creatures: Sniper (1), Rejuvenator (1), 3 tokens (1,1,1) = 5 power. They block 1 or 2 with Baloth and Cultivator, ~3 damage through. They go to 8. Keep Warmaster safe.\n\
\n\
Or... attack with all 6 but if they block Warmaster with Baloth, Warmaster (2) doesn't kill Baloth (3 toughness) and Baloth (4) kills Warmaster. Very bad.\n\
\n\
Better: Equip Bow to Warmaster (3 mana), making it 3/4. Then attack. If they block with Baloth, both trade (3 vs 3 toughness, 4 vs 4 toughness). Warmaster + Bow for their Baloth. Not ideal but removes their threat.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me use Band Together differently. Can I target TWO creatures to deal damage? \"Up to two target creatures you control each deal damage equal to their power to another target creature.\" So two 1/1 tokens deal 1+1=2 to Baloth. Not enough.\n\
\n\
Warmaster (2) + any 1/1 = 3. Still need 4.\n\
\n\
What if I equip Bow to a token first? Token becomes 2/3. Then Band Together: token (2) + Warmaster (2) = 4 damage to Baloth! But equip (3) + Band Together (3) = 6 mana. Only have 5.\n\
\n\
Okay, I can't kill Baloth this turn with the tools I have. Best play:\n\
\n\
Option A: Wildheart Invoker (4 mana) — add a 4/3. Attack with small stuff, hold Warmaster back. \n\
Option B: Equip Bow to Warmaster (3 mana) — Warmaster becomes 3/4 with reach. Attack with Warmaster, if they block with Baloth they trade. Then play something with remaining 2 mana — nothing useful.\n\
\n\
I think Option A is better. Invoker is a 4/3 that can't be attacked past, and next turn I'll have 6 mana for Band Together or other plays. Plus it doesn't risk Warmaster.",
