Non-sick attackers: 3 Elf tokens (1/1), Rejuvenator (1/1), Warmaster (2/2), Sniper (1/2) = 7 power.\n\
Opponents blockers: Baloth (4/3) and Cultivator (0/3).\n\
\n\
I'll attack with everything EXCEPT Warmaster. I want to keep Warmaster alive.\n\
\n\
5 attackers: 3 tokens + Rejuvenator + Sniper = 5 power.\n\
- If they double block, they kill 2 creatures but I still push through some damage.\n\
- If Baloth blocks Sniper (1/2), Sniper dies. Cultivator blocks a token. 3 damage through. Opponent goes to 8.\n\
- If Baloth blocks a token, token dies. Cultivator blocks another. 3 damage through (Sniper + Rejuvenator + 1 token). Same result.\n\
\n\
Actually, they'll likely put Baloth on something and Cultivator on something. Max 2 blocked, so 3 creatures get through = 3 damage minimum. Opponent goes from 11 to 8.\n\
\n\
Or I could send Warmaster too for 7 power total. They block 2, 5 gets through. But risking Warmaster to Baloth...\n\
\n\
If Baloth blocks Warmaster: Warmaster (2) doesn't kill Baloth (3 toughness). Baloth (4) kills Warmaster. Terrible.\n\
\n\
Keep Warmaster back. Send the other 5.",
