      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 42,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed with 3 untapped lands and nothing else to do, wasting the opportunity to sacrifice Oashra Cultivator for ramp. Activating it now would provide 5 mana next turn, enabling a turn-7 Garruk, Unleashed alongside a land drop, rather than having to wait. The 0/3 body provides minimal value as a blocker against the opponent's growing elf army.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without using any mana, doing nothing this turn.",
      "better_line": "Activate Oashra Cultivator ({2}{G}, tap, sacrifice) to search for a basic land, ramping to 5 mana next turn to enable casting Garruk, Unleashed or Canopy Baloth + equip Adventuring Gear.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 70,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 47,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed on casting Elven Bow with the only remaining untapped mana when no other spells in hand could be cast for just {G}. The Bow would enter unattached (can't pay {2} for the token), but would be on the battlefield ready to equip later, providing +1/+2 and reach to any creature. Since Band Together and Titanic Growth both require more than 1 mana, there's no reason to hold up the green mana.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, wasting 1 available green mana with no instant-speed plays possible.",
      "better_line": "Cast Elven Bow for {G} to get it onto the battlefield for future equipping. No combat tricks are castable with just 1 mana anyway, so there's no bluffing or reactive value in holding it open.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 97,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "decision_index": 62,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT53C Teach passed priority in postcombat main phase with an unplayed Thriving Grove in hand and a land drop remaining. Playing the land would have given them 4 mana sources next turn (important for casting Garruk, Unleashed next turn which costs 2GG, or Canopy Baloth). Additionally, playing the land would trigger Adventuring Gear's landfall if equipped to a creature, though currently nothing is equipped. More importantly, the extra mana is pure upside - there's no reason not to play the Thriving Grove.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without playing Thriving Grove.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Grove (choosing no additional color needed since the deck appears mono-green), giving access to 4 mana next turn to cast Garruk, Unleashed or Canopy Baloth.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 121,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 78,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "GPT53C Teach declined to attack with Garruk's Harbinger (4/3) when the opponent had very limited blocking options (mostly summoning sick 1/1s and a 2/2). More critically, they had Hunter's Insight in hand with exactly 3 mana available - attacking and casting Hunter's Insight on an unblocked Harbinger would draw 4 cards AND trigger Harbinger's ability to find a creature. Even if blocked by the 2/2 Dwynen's Elite, the Harbinger survives and kills the blocker. This was a massive missed opportunity for card advantage.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to attack with any creatures.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Garruk's Harbinger, then if unblocked cast Hunter's Insight on it to draw 4 cards and trigger Harbinger's ability. Even without Hunter's Insight, the attack is profitable since the opponent's best blocker is a 2/2 that trades unfavorably with the 4/3.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 122,
      "player": "GPT53C Teach",
      "decision_index": 79,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "All of the opponent's creatures are either tapped or have summoning sickness, meaning Garruk's Harbinger 4/3 is guaranteed to connect for combat damage. Casting Hunter's Insight targeting the Harbinger before attacks would draw 4 cards when it deals combat damage — an enormous card advantage swing in Limited. The player had exactly 3 untapped Forests to cast it.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Hunter's Insight, missing a guaranteed 4-card draw.",
      "better_line": "Cast Hunter's Insight targeting Garruk's Harbinger, then attack with it for an unblockable 4 damage and draw 4 cards.",
